{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["May He who implants the spirit in a trusting son, who dwells in the heart of a clear-thinking person—he will teach me to grasp hidden things; the acquisition of intellect he apportioned bright, rejecting the sour, hating the arrogant—my portion is Ezra the swift scribe." "<b>And in the year</b> — The word בשנת is attached to the word אחת, for every number-noun and every thing-noun is two [construct], except to indicate in which time of the counting of the units it was so; thus the matter is supported by one of the numbers, as we find בשנת שלש, בשנת שבע. Also the numbers are attached to nouns, to inform and to indicate from them what the things are, as we said: שני אנשים, שלשת הנפת, ארבעת ימים, שמונת הבקר. And the meaning of בשנת אחת למלכו על בבל is that previously he was king of Persia. And the word אחת—the grammarians said that it is deficient of dalet, [i.e.,] אחדת, and the primary letters, which are דג\"ז קט\"ף ע\"ץ חס\"ד, are never reduced, except for the doubled ones resembling ayin and lamed. But the correct view is that אחד for masculine and אחת for feminine are two forms in one matter and two roots; likewise אחד עשר and עשתי עשר in one matter." "<b>To Cyrus</b> — Some say that the word is inverted from וכשר, and the matter is fitting, for the prophet Isaiah already called him by his name on account of the merit he would do for Israel, and this is what he said: 'He shall build My city and he shall send out My exiles.'" "<b>To fulfill</b> — At the time of fulfilling the word of HaShem that went forth from the mouth of Jeremiah, to visit them upon the completion of the kingdom of Babylon's seventy years, and to bring them out from servitude. For thus it is written in Chronicles: 'And they shall be servants to him and to his sons until the kingdom of Persia reigns.' For in the first year of Cyrus they were fifty-two [years] since the destruction of Jerusalem, and the Temple service ceased, until the land had desire of its sabbaths. And in the second year of Darius, seventy years were completed since the destruction of the Holy City, for thus it is written: 'against which you have raged these seventy years.'" "<b>HaShem stirred up his spirit</b> — To build His city." "<b>And also by letter</b> — It was sealed with his signet."], :book :ezra, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Ezra -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/ezra"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:41:39.788144250Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}